specialFamiliesOfSommeseVandeVen -- produce a member of the special family
**************************************************************************

  * Usage: 
        Y=specialFamiliesOfSommeseVandeVen(kk,fam)
  * Inputs:
      * kk, a *note ring: (Macaulay2Doc)Ring,, the ground field
      * fam, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, number of the family
  * Outputs:
      * Y, an *note ideal: (Macaulay2Doc)Ideal,, the ideal of a surface

Description
===========

By [SVdV] four families of smooth surfaces Y behave differently in the
adjunction process: |H+K_Y| defines a morphism Y -> Y_1 which is generically
finite to 1 instead of birational. These families are

1) P2(6;2p_1,...,2p_7)

2) P2(6;2p_1,...,2p_7,p_8)

3) P2(9;3p_1,...,3p_8)

4) Y=P(E) where E is a indecomposable rank 2 vector bundle over an elliptic
curve and H=3B, where B in Y is the section with B^2=1.



